# The room's map, written the way it looks: the first row here is the top row on screen.
#
# 0 is floor, 1 is wall, 2 is the threshold under the way out and 3 is the rug the walker
# starts on. Only 1 blocks, and which id does is `room:tiles.hall`'s business rather than
# this file's -- a package loaded after it could make the rug solid without touching a
# single number here.
#
# Thirty-two cells by twenty-four, which at the zoom the settings ask for is larger than
# the window. That is deliberate: a map that fits on screen never asks the camera to
# follow anything, and following is most of what makes a room feel like a place.
#
# The doorway is the two-cell gap in row 6. Nothing here says a door stands in it -- that
# is `room:door.north`, an entity, because a door has to be able to stop existing.
#
# `fpack` compiles this to `grids/hall.fgrid` and mints `room:grids.hall` from the path.
# Nothing at runtime ever asks for either filename (ADR-0021).

